{"id":"mahabharata-12-094","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":94,"title":"चतुर्नवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 94 · Vamadeva's counsel to a king","summary":{"en":"The sage Vamadeva tells a king that he who uses force against the weak lives on a wicked livelihood, and he describes the king's helpers, officers and ministers whom he must trust. He ends with the secret teaching of kings which Yayati spoke.","kn":"ದುರ್ಬಲರ ಮೇಲೆ ಬಲ ಬಳಸುವವನು ಕೆಟ್ಟ ವೃತ್ತಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಬದುಕುತ್ತಾನೆಂದು ವಾಮದೇವ ಋಷಿ ರಾಜನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳಿ ರಾಜ ನಂಬಬೇಕಾದ ಸಹಾಯಕ, ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ, ಮಂತ್ರಿಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯಯಾತಿ ಹೇಳಿದ ರಾಜೋಪನಿಷತ್ತಿನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"ऋषि वामदेव राजा से कहते हैं कि दुर्बल पर बल प्रयोग करने वाला बुरी जीविका जीता है, और वे राजा के विश्वसनीय सहायकों, अधिकारियों और मन्त्रियों का वर्णन करते हैं। वे ययाति द्वारा कही राजोपनिषद् के साथ समाप्त करते हैं।","te":"బలహీనునిపై బలం ప్రయోగించేవాడు చెడ్డ జీవనం సాగిస్తాడని వామదేవ ఋషి రాజుకు చెప్పి రాజు నమ్మవలసిన సహాయకులు, అధికారులు, మంత్రులను వర్ణిస్తాడు. యయాతి చెప్పిన రాజోపనిషత్తుతో ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"மெலியோர் மீது வன்மை செலுத்துபவன் தீய வாழ்வு வாழ்கிறான் என்று முனிவர் வாமதேவர் மன்னனுக்குக் கூறி, மன்னன் நம்ப வேண்டிய உதவியாளர், அதிகாரிகள், அமைச்சரை விவரிக்கிறார். யயாதி கூறிய ராஜோபநிஷத்துடன் முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ദുർബലരോട് ബലം പ്രയോഗിക്കുന്നവൻ ദുഷ്ടമായ ജീവിതമാണ് നയിക്കുന്നതെന്ന് വാമദേവൻ എന്ന മുനി ഒരു രാജാവിനോട് പറയുന്നു; രാജാവ് വിശ്വസിക്കേണ്ട സഹായികളെയും ഉദ്യോഗസ്ഥരെയും മന്ത്രിമാരെയും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. യയാതി പറഞ്ഞ രാജാക്കന്മാരുടെ രഹസ്യോപദേശത്തോടെ അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.94; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यत्राधर्मं प्रणयते दुर्बले बलवत्तरः ।\nतां वृत्तिमुपजीवन्ति ये भवन्ति तदन्वयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where a stronger man does wrong to a weaker one, those who live off that way of life and belong to that circle follow such a king, the promoter of sin, and a kingdom of undisciplined people soon perishes."}},{"n":2,"text":"राजानमनुवर्तन्ते तं पापाभिप्रवर्तकम् ।\nअविनीतमनुष्यं तत्क्षिप्रं राष्ट्रं विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the powerful treat the weak unjustly, those around the king who live by that conduct follow him, and such a kingdom whose people lack discipline is quickly ruined."}},{"n":3,"text":"यद्वृत्तिमुपजीवन्ति प्रकृतिस्थस्य मानवाः ।\nतदेव विषमस्थस्य स्वजनोऽपि न मृष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The livelihood that people enjoy under a king who keeps to his nature, even his own kin will not tolerate when it is taken away from one who has fallen into hardship."}},{"n":4,"text":"साहसप्रकृतिर्यत्र कुरुते किंचिदुल्बणम् ।\nअशास्त्रलक्षणो राजा क्षिप्रमेव विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king of rash temperament who does some violent act and bears none of the marks of scriptural guidance is swiftly destroyed."}},{"n":5,"text":"योऽत्यन्ताचरितां वृत्तिं क्षत्रियो नानुवर्तते ।\nजितानामजितानां च क्षत्रधर्मादपैति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Kshatriya who does not follow the long-practised conduct toward the conquered and the unconquered falls away from the duty of a warrior."}},{"n":6,"text":"द्विषन्तं कृतकर्माणं गृहीत्वा नृपती रणे ।\nयो न मानयते द्वेषात्क्षत्रधर्मादपैति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who captures in battle an enemy who has done his deed and then, out of hatred, shows him no respect, falls away from the duty of a warrior."}},{"n":7,"text":"शक्तः स्यात्सुमुखो राजा कुर्यात्कारुण्यमापदि ।\nप्रियो भवति भूतानां न च विभ्रश्यते श्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A capable king should have a gracious face and show compassion in misfortune; he becomes dear to creatures and does not lose his fortune."}},{"n":8,"text":"अप्रियं यस्य कुर्वीत भूयस्तस्य प्रियं चरेत् ।\nनचिरेण प्रियः स स्याद्योऽप्रियः प्रियमाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"To one who has been made to suffer by you, do even more kindness; whoever returns kindness for unkindness soon becomes dear."}},{"n":9,"text":"मृषावादं परिहरेत्कुर्यात्प्रियमयाचितः ।\nन च कामान्न संरम्भान्न द्वेषाद्धर्ममुत्सृजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should avoid falsehood and do favours unasked, and never abandon dharma for desire, anger or hatred."}},{"n":10,"text":"नापत्रपेत प्रश्नेषु नाभिभव्यां गिरं सृजेत् ।\nन त्वरेत न चासूयेत्तथा संगृह्यते परः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not be ashamed when questioned, nor speak in an overbearing voice; he should not be hasty or envious, and so wins over others."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रिये नातिभृशं हृष्येदप्रिये न च संज्वरेत् ।\nन मुह्येदर्थकृच्छ्रेषु प्रजाहितमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not rejoice too much at what is pleasant nor burn at what is unpleasant, and in hard affairs he should not lose his head, keeping the welfare of his subjects in mind."}},{"n":12,"text":"यः प्रियं कुरुते नित्यं गुणतो वसुधाधिपः ।\nतस्य कर्माणि सिध्यन्ति न च संत्यज्यते श्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who always does what is good for others, according to their merits, sees his undertakings succeed and is never abandoned by prosperity."}},{"n":13,"text":"निवृत्तं प्रतिकूलेभ्यो वर्तमानमनुप्रिये ।\nभक्तं भजेत नृपतिस्तद्वै वृत्तं सतामिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should favour the devoted man who keeps away from what is hostile and lives to please; that is indeed the conduct of the good in this world."}},{"n":14,"text":"अप्रकीर्णेन्द्रियं प्राज्ञमत्यन्तानुगतं शुचिम् ।\nशक्तं चैवानुरक्तं च युञ्ज्यान्महति कर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should appoint to great work one wise, pure, able and loyal, whose senses are not scattered and who is wholly devoted."}},{"n":15,"text":"एवमेव गुणैर्युक्तो यो न रज्यति भूमिपम् ।\nभर्तुरर्थेष्वसूयन्तं न तं युञ्जीत कर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But one who has such qualities yet is not attached to the king, and who resents his master's interests, should not be given any post."}},{"n":16,"text":"मूढमैन्द्रियकं लुब्धमनार्यचरितं शठम् ।\nअनतीतोपधं हिंस्रं दुर्बुद्धिमबहुश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fool, a slave of the senses, a greedy man, one of ignoble conduct, a cheat, a deceiver, a violent and dull-witted man with little learning..."}},{"n":17,"text":"त्यक्तोपात्तं मद्यरतं द्यूतस्त्रीमृगयापरम् ।\nकार्ये महति यो युञ्ज्याद्धीयते स नृपः श्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...one who has given up what he took up, given to drink, dice, women and hunting: the king who appoints such a man to a great task loses his fortune."}},{"n":18,"text":"रक्षितात्मा तु यो राजा रक्ष्यान्यश्चानुरक्षति ।\nप्रजाश्च तस्य वर्धन्ते ध्रुवं च महदश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who guards himself and also guards those who need protection sees his subjects prosper and gains great things for certain."}},{"n":19,"text":"ये केचिद्भूमिपतयस्तान्सर्वानन्ववेक्षयेत् ।\nसुहृद्भिरनभिख्यातैस्तेन राजा न रिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should keep watch over all the kings of the earth through friends who go unrecognised; by this a king does not come to harm."}},{"n":20,"text":"अपकृत्य बलस्थस्य दूरस्थोऽस्मीति नाश्वसेत् ।\nश्येनानुचरितैर्ह्येते निपतन्ति प्रमाद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having wronged a strong man, do not feel safe thinking 'I am far away'; such men swoop down like hawks on one who is careless."}},{"n":21,"text":"दृढमूलस्त्वदुष्टात्मा विदित्वा बलमात्मनः ।\nअबलानभियुञ्जीत न तु ये बलवत्तराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One with firm roots and a blameless heart, knowing his own strength, should attack the weak and not those who are stronger."}},{"n":22,"text":"विक्रमेण महीं लब्ध्वा प्रजा धर्मेण पालयन् ।\nआहवे निधनं कुर्याद्राजा धर्मपरायणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king devoted to dharma, who wins the earth by valour and protects his people by righteousness, may meet his death in battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"मरणान्तमिदं सर्वं नेह किंचिदनामयम् ।\nतस्माद्धर्मे स्थितो राजा प्रजा धर्मेण पालयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this ends in death; nothing here is free from affliction. So a king who stands in dharma should protect his people by dharma."}},{"n":24,"text":"रक्षाधिकरणं युद्धं तथा धर्मानुशासनम् ।\nमन्त्रचिन्त्यं सुखं काले पञ्चभिर्वर्धते मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"Protection, war, the teaching of dharma, deliberation in counsel and happiness in due season: by these five the earth prospers."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतानि यस्य गुप्तानि स राजा राजसत्तम ।\nसततं वर्तमानोऽत्र राजा भुङ्क्ते महीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who keeps these safeguarded, best of kings, and always conducts himself so, enjoys this earth."}},{"n":26,"text":"नैतान्येकेन शक्यानि सातत्येनान्ववेक्षितुम् ।\nएतेष्वाप्तान्प्रतिष्ठाप्य राजा भुङ्क्ते महीं चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One man alone cannot keep watching over all these constantly; by placing trustworthy men over them a king enjoys the earth long."}},{"n":27,"text":"दातारं संविभक्तारं मार्दवोपगतं शुचिम् ।\nअसंत्यक्तमनुष्यं च तं जनाः कुर्वते प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"People hold dear a man who gives, shares with others, is gentle and pure, and does not abandon his men."}},{"n":28,"text":"यस्तु निःश्रेयसं ज्ञात्वा ज्ञानं तत्प्रतिपद्यते ।\nआत्मनो मतमुत्सृज्य तं लोकोऽनुविधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who knows what is best and takes up the knowledge, setting aside his own opinion, is followed by the world."}},{"n":29,"text":"योऽर्थकामस्य वचनं प्रातिकूल्यान्न मृष्यते ।\nशृणोति प्रतिकूलानि विमना नचिरादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, out of dislike, cannot bear the words of a well-wisher and listens to unwelcome things with displeasure soon..."}},{"n":30,"text":"अग्राम्यचरितां बुद्धिमत्यन्तं यो न बुध्यते ।\nजितानामजितानां च क्षत्रधर्मादपैति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who does not fully grasp the understanding that is free from vulgar conduct falls away from the warrior's duty toward the conquered and unconquered."}},{"n":31,"text":"मुख्यानमात्यान्यो हित्वा निहीनान्कुरुते प्रियान् ।\nस वै व्यसनमासाद्य गाधमार्तो न विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who abandons the chief ministers and makes favourites of lesser men, once in trouble, finds no footing, like a distressed man in deep water."}},{"n":32,"text":"यः कल्याणगुणाञ्ज्ञातीन्द्वेषान्नैवाभिमन्यते ।\nअदृढात्मा दृढक्रोधो नास्यार्थो रमतेऽन्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who out of hatred does not honour kinsmen of excellent qualities, weak in mind yet fierce in anger, finds wealth does not stay near him."}},{"n":33,"text":"अथ यो गुणसंपन्नान्हृदयस्याप्रियानपि ।\nप्रियेण कुरुते वश्यांश्चिरं यशसि तिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But he who makes subject to himself, through kindness, even those with good qualities who are not dear to his heart, stands long in fame."}},{"n":34,"text":"नाकाले प्रणयेदर्थान्नाप्रिये जातु संज्वरेत् ।\nप्रिये नातिभृशं हृष्येद्युज्येतारोग्यकर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not pursue his aims at the wrong time, never burn with anger at what is disagreeable, not rejoice too much at the agreeable, and should engage in health-giving practice."}},{"n":35,"text":"के मानुरक्ता राजानः के भयात्समुपाश्रिताः ।\nमध्यस्थदोषाः के चैषामिति नित्यं विचिन्तयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should always reflect: which kings are truly attached to me, which have come to me from fear, and which are neutral with their faults?"}},{"n":36,"text":"न जातु बलवान्भूत्वा दुर्बले विश्वसेत्क्वचित् ।\nभारुण्डसदृशा ह्येते निपतन्ति प्रमाद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Never, having become strong, should one trust a weak man; such men fall upon the careless like bharunda birds."}},{"n":37,"text":"अपि सर्वैर्गुणैर्युक्तं भर्तारं प्रियवादिनम् ।\nअभिद्रुह्यति पापात्मा तस्माद्धि विभिषेज्जनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a master endowed with every virtue and sweet of speech is betrayed by a wicked man, so one should be wary of people."}},{"n":38,"text":"एतां राजोपनिषदं ययातिः स्माह नाहुषः ।\nमनुष्यविजये युक्तो हन्ति शत्रूननुत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This secret teaching for kings was spoken by Yayati, son of Nahusha; a king engaged in conquering men destroys his unrivalled foes."}}]}]}